## Verification

`mise run check` is the fast quality gate. Use `mise run verify` for product,
integration, browser, artifact, or other claims that need more than formatting,
static analysis, and unit tests. It runs `check`, stack-specific verification,
and any required product routes.

Add a route only after exercising a real feature or caller journey. Register its
source and dependency paths in `.harness/verification.toml`, then use a focused
route while iterating:

```bash
scripts/verify-routes --path src/records/api.py
mise run verify -- --path src/records/api.py
```

With no path selector, `mise run verify` runs every required automated route.
Keep manual or credentialed checks as explicit operator evidence; do not mark
them as automated passes.

## Task Reference

| Command | Purpose |
|---------|---------|
| `mise run setup` | Install dependencies and prepare the environment |
| `mise run fmt` | Auto-format code |
| `mise run lint` | Run lint checks (non-modifying) |
| `mise run typecheck` | Run static type analysis |
| `mise run test` | Run unit tests |
| `mise run build` | Build artifacts |
| `mise run check` | Fast quality gate (fmt + lint + typecheck + test) |
| `mise run verify` | Heavy validation and selected product verification routes |
{% if project_shape == "apps" %}| `mise run dev -- <module>` | Start local development for a module |{% else %}| `mise run dev` | Start local development |{% endif %}
| `mise run ci` | CI entrypoint (= check) |

